      "side": 1,
      "message": "Copying over notes from the [Google Doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GCioZymU01gacga2PKk3olM4KHvSVpeZyHVQ2b7NwUQ/edit?tab\u003dt.0) about the workflow UX challenges we should try to solve in this change (or immediate follow-ups):\n\n* Users need to *know* that the project is SPAM-protected and where/how to ask (or who?) for permission to post comments\n* It looks like the SPAM-protected workflow risks being a bad user experience vs. the current workflow\n* We currently have a similar issue for uploading changes (users cannot upload and wonder why?)\n* Can we just resolve it with a nice error message? This should be project-specific (perhaps a text field in the project settings), as different projects may have different policies for preventing SPAMers.\n* What could a default workflow look like?\n  - Provide a “button” to request to be unblocked and be able to comment\n  - The “button” sends an e-mail to someone and they add you to a group\n  - Possible enhanced/plugin version: Pressing the button triggers a “CAPTCHA” to demonstrate you are a human and then you’re added to the group automatically (project owner configures which group in the project settings?)\n  - Other possible enhanced version: Pressing the button triggers a “request to be added to group” workflow (new Gerrit feature) and the project/group owner approves the request",
